WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.091
[discordant, suspenseful music playing]

00:11.011 --> 00:15.015
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

00:16.016 --> 00:17.100
[music continues]

00:18.393 --> 00:19.894
Are you suggesting

00:20.729 --> 00:22.439
that I should fabricate the truth?

00:22.522 --> 00:25.150
-[Mun-oh] What? Where'd you get that?
-We don't have evidence.

00:25.650 --> 00:28.570
You want me to pretend
I saw Mr. Kim kill Min-hui.

00:29.070 --> 00:31.614
I wasn't at the hospital.
I didn't see anyone or observe--

00:31.698 --> 00:33.199
Enough! Just shut your mouth!

00:33.283 --> 00:34.409
[breathing agitatedly]

00:35.076 --> 00:37.704
You weren't at the hospital,
but you know what happened there.

00:38.538 --> 00:41.124
It's not lying if you know the truth.

00:41.207 --> 00:44.711
And the truth is,
Su-hun went to meet the letter-writer.

00:44.794 --> 00:46.629
He basically admitted
to committing the crime

00:46.713 --> 00:49.716
when he showed up
to discuss the security footage.

00:49.799 --> 00:50.884
That's what counts.

00:50.967 --> 00:53.762
And you were at the park
to witness that yourself, Lee Kang!

00:55.805 --> 00:56.639
[music abates]

00:58.099 --> 01:00.643
Hey. Why are you so quiet?

01:04.064 --> 01:06.941
Because I wouldn't be writing
about my own experience.

01:07.025 --> 01:09.486
This would be the opposite
of what you've been telling me.

01:09.569 --> 01:13.198
All this time you've been teaching me,
you said a writer must be objective,

01:13.281 --> 01:15.492
that we have to depict reality as it is.

01:15.575 --> 01:18.828
This is real, and you can write it.

01:19.329 --> 01:22.123
You're not concocting evidence or lying.

01:22.624 --> 01:25.627
You're just taking a little
creative license to round out the story.

01:25.710 --> 01:26.753
That's all.

01:26.836 --> 01:28.922
Artistic liberty is not fraud.

01:29.005 --> 01:30.673
You don't need the whole truth.

01:30.757 --> 01:33.968
This is when a writer needs to decide
if this truth is important.

01:36.429 --> 01:38.014
[Kang] I don't know, Professor.

01:39.390 --> 01:41.476
What's the point
of putting that out there?

01:41.559 --> 01:43.311
The world needs this story.

01:43.978 --> 01:46.356
Kim Su-hun has gotten away with murder.

01:47.857 --> 01:50.193
An author has a duty
to go where the story leads.

01:50.693 --> 01:52.153
[Kang sighs]

01:52.237 --> 01:53.071
I know.

01:54.572 --> 01:55.990
But I'm afraid I can't.

01:56.491 --> 01:59.869
I don't have the energy to finish it.
I'm too worried about my dad.

02:00.370 --> 02:02.330
[breathes shakily]

02:02.914 --> 02:05.291
He's not doing so great,
and he really needs me.

02:06.543 --> 02:09.587
Would you mind being the one
who puts the final touches on the story?

02:09.671 --> 02:11.131
You mean, I would write it?

02:11.214 --> 02:12.257
[uneasy music playing]

02:12.340 --> 02:16.010
Why wouldn't you?
I'm not the author here. Come on!

02:16.094 --> 02:18.638
[Kang] But you are an author,
a published one.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.517
Please do this
or it'll never get finished.

02:23.017 --> 02:24.435
I'm begging you, sir.

02:25.353 --> 02:26.896
Finish my story. Please.

02:26.980 --> 02:29.315
Wait a second!
Hey! Hey! Don't be an idiot!

02:29.399 --> 02:32.068
-Lee Kang, don't you dare hang up on m--
-[line clicks]

02:32.694 --> 02:34.863
Bastard! Who the hell
do you think you are?

02:34.946 --> 02:36.114
God dammit!

02:36.197 --> 02:37.407
[breathing heavily]

02:40.034 --> 02:40.869
[groans]

02:41.494 --> 02:42.412
[shouts]

02:43.997 --> 02:45.206
[breathing heavily]

02:49.544 --> 02:50.420
[whimpers]

02:54.966 --> 02:56.217
[breathing softens]

03:05.435 --> 03:06.519
What did he say?

03:11.482 --> 03:13.151
I should finish the story?

03:14.110 --> 03:16.029
[somber, contemplative music playing]

03:34.547 --> 03:35.673
[breathes agitatedly]

03:43.223 --> 03:44.182
I…

03:45.767 --> 03:47.477
need to finish the story.

03:56.611 --> 03:57.820
[breathing softens]

04:00.573 --> 04:02.116
I'm the author now.

04:06.287 --> 04:07.372
[music rises, abates]

04:07.455 --> 04:11.251
I had trouble understanding
what the writer was attempting to say.

04:12.502 --> 04:13.878
Honestly, I thought,

04:14.671 --> 04:17.423
why would you bother writing
without saying anything?

04:19.259 --> 04:21.344
There's nothing wrong with that, you know?

04:22.971 --> 04:25.014
But most of all, you should

04:25.974 --> 04:28.017
revisit how to write good sentences.

04:28.685 --> 04:30.645
[jazzy, percussive music playing]

04:35.275 --> 04:37.026
-[breathes heavily]
-[music abates]

04:39.904 --> 04:41.072
Son of a bitch.

04:41.155 --> 04:43.116
Kim Su-hun, are you ready?

04:43.866 --> 04:45.076
[exhales shakily]

04:45.159 --> 04:47.203
Because I'll show you no mercy this time.

04:47.287 --> 04:48.663
[kinetic jazz playing]

04:52.583 --> 04:54.043
[keyboard clacking rapidly]

05:15.982 --> 05:17.150
[music intensifies]

05:17.233 --> 05:18.568
[breathing excitedly]

05:20.486 --> 05:22.030
[breathy indistinct muttering]

05:30.246 --> 05:31.789
[manic laughter]

05:32.415 --> 05:33.750
[keyboard clacking]

05:40.256 --> 05:41.382
[music swells]

05:45.470 --> 05:46.596
[music abates]

05:49.098 --> 05:51.309
[children at play shouting in distance]

05:53.644 --> 05:56.147
[passing motorbike rumbles faintly]

05:57.190 --> 05:58.399
[music fades]

06:03.071 --> 06:06.449
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW
BY HEO MUN-OH

06:06.532 --> 06:08.493
[coughs]

06:10.203 --> 06:11.829
[coughing]

06:15.666 --> 06:16.876
[inhales deeply]

06:16.959 --> 06:18.586
[coughs]

06:19.379 --> 06:20.671
[exhales groggily]

06:21.172 --> 06:22.131
[grunts]

06:24.300 --> 06:25.885
[groans]

06:27.720 --> 06:28.721
[sighs]

06:29.889 --> 06:30.890
[groans]

06:34.602 --> 06:36.354
[exhales deeply]

06:40.858 --> 06:42.652
[soft, wistful piano music playing]

06:46.614 --> 06:48.074
[sighs] Oh God.

06:49.951 --> 06:51.494
I didn't imagine it.

06:57.250 --> 06:58.292
I did it.

06:58.793 --> 07:00.253
I finally did it.

07:01.629 --> 07:02.713
Heo Mun-oh.

07:09.595 --> 07:11.097
My second novel.

07:12.098 --> 07:13.391
[breathes heavily]

07:14.475 --> 07:15.977
[cell phone vibrating]

07:20.898 --> 07:22.150
[vibrating continues]

07:30.366 --> 07:31.325
[grunts]

07:34.203 --> 07:35.246
[sighs]

07:36.497 --> 07:38.416
-[grunts softly]
-[vibrating continues]

07:41.210 --> 07:42.295
[chuckles softly]

07:42.795 --> 07:43.713
[vibrating stops]

07:44.297 --> 07:48.134
Oh, well, look who it is.
Calling at the crack of dawn after you--

07:48.217 --> 07:49.510
-[Kang] Professor!
-You hung up--

07:49.594 --> 07:51.971
[Kang] I've been trying
to get a hold of you for hours!

07:53.389 --> 07:55.808
If you keep yelling like that,
I'm gonna hang up this instant.

07:55.892 --> 07:57.185
You've got some nerve, kid--

07:57.268 --> 07:59.604
[Kang] Do you know
how many times I've called you?

07:59.687 --> 08:00.563
What?

08:03.065 --> 08:04.901
LEE KANG
13 MISSED CALLS

08:07.737 --> 08:09.864
Thirteen? What's going on?

08:09.947 --> 08:11.532
[breathing anxiously]

08:11.616 --> 08:12.575
It's crazy.

08:13.075 --> 08:16.370
Promise you'll try not to lose it
when you hear what I'm about to say.

08:17.163 --> 08:19.499
You know the last scene
at the hospital we talked about?

08:19.582 --> 08:21.375
Well, that scene isn't how it ends.

08:21.459 --> 08:24.837
There's an even scarier one,
and I think it's happening right now!

08:24.921 --> 08:26.339
[soft, uneasy music playing]

08:26.422 --> 08:29.300
W… w… what are you talking about?
You're not making sense.

08:32.929 --> 08:35.181
-[tires screeching]
-[engine revs]

08:35.264 --> 08:36.390
[dramatic music playing]

08:38.184 --> 08:40.895
-[tires screech]
-[passing car horn honks]

08:44.232 --> 08:45.399
[engine revs]

08:45.483 --> 08:46.692
[car horn honks]

08:47.527 --> 08:48.444
[Mon-oh honks horn]

08:48.528 --> 08:50.279
Move it! Come on! Shit!

08:50.363 --> 08:51.656
[tires screech]

08:51.739 --> 08:52.782
[engine revs]

08:52.865 --> 08:54.659
[nearby car horn honking]

08:59.455 --> 09:00.540
[music continues]

09:01.541 --> 09:04.919
[Kang] I woke up really early, and I saw
that I missed a call from Se-yun.

09:05.002 --> 09:06.254
SE-YUN
2 MISSED CALLS

09:09.757 --> 09:11.968
I had a bad feeling, so I called him back.

09:12.051 --> 09:15.429
[automated voice] The person you are
trying to call is not available. Please…

09:17.890 --> 09:18.975
[music abates]

09:21.185 --> 09:22.728
[foreboding music drones]

09:25.773 --> 09:27.984
[Se-yun breathing shakily] Kang! Kang!

09:28.067 --> 09:29.443
[banging in background]

09:29.527 --> 09:31.237
[hushed] Kang. Kang!

09:32.363 --> 09:33.447
Kang…

09:33.531 --> 09:35.449
-[breathes shakily]
-[banging on door]

09:38.744 --> 09:40.538
It's Se-yun. Are you listening?

09:41.038 --> 09:42.790
-[banging intensifies]
-[gasps]

09:42.873 --> 09:44.333
[rattling violently]

09:44.417 --> 09:45.251
[banging]

09:45.334 --> 09:47.545
It's my dad. He's trying to kill us.

09:47.628 --> 09:48.629
-[banging]
-[gasps]

09:48.713 --> 09:50.006
[door handle rattling]

09:50.089 --> 09:53.593
[sobs] He's planning to start a fire
to burn the house down.

09:55.136 --> 09:56.762
He's burning the house down?

09:57.305 --> 09:58.514
With her in it?

09:59.599 --> 10:01.309
He's murdering his wife and son?

10:01.392 --> 10:04.895
[Kang] The end of the message
is horrifying. It chilled me to the bone.

10:05.396 --> 10:06.522
[rattling]

10:07.023 --> 10:08.399
[handle clatters outside]

10:10.443 --> 10:12.069
[suspenseful music playing]

10:12.153 --> 10:14.071
[Su-hun breathing heavily]

10:19.577 --> 10:20.620
[huffs deeply]

10:24.165 --> 10:25.583
[music intensifying]

10:25.666 --> 10:26.959
[cell phone clatters]

10:27.877 --> 10:28.919
[Se-yun gasps]

10:36.093 --> 10:37.345
[Se-yun breathes shakily]

10:38.971 --> 10:40.056
[music peaks, abates]

10:40.931 --> 10:42.266
[Su-hun breathing heavily]

10:44.101 --> 10:45.061
Is that…

10:45.936 --> 10:47.938
[heavy, shaky breathing]

10:53.611 --> 10:54.445
[Se-yun screams]

10:54.528 --> 10:55.696
[dull thud echoes]

10:55.780 --> 10:57.406
[tense, intriguing music playing]

10:58.240 --> 11:00.242
[Kang] That sound
is the last thing I heard.

11:00.326 --> 11:01.661
[Mun-oh's breath trembles]

11:03.663 --> 11:06.415
[sighs] I don't know
if they're still alive.

11:07.333 --> 11:09.460
[sobs] I'm so scared, Professor.

11:09.543 --> 11:10.378
[sniffles]

11:11.003 --> 11:12.421
[sobbing]

11:12.505 --> 11:15.716
[grumbles] I think he found out
that Eun-joo knew what he's been up to,

11:15.800 --> 11:17.760
and he can't let his secret get out.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.013
[sighs] He's desperate.

11:21.514 --> 11:23.265
He stands to lose everything.

11:23.349 --> 11:24.934
[Kang] I'm going to the house.

11:25.017 --> 11:28.771
But it'll take me a while to get back
to the city, so I was hoping you could

11:29.271 --> 11:32.733
do me a favor and go there yourself,
maybe before it's too late.

11:32.817 --> 11:35.695
Yes, of course. I'm going.
Just text me the address.

11:35.778 --> 11:37.029
[tense music continues]

11:38.572 --> 11:40.408
You measly fucking coward.

11:41.325 --> 11:43.369
You'd rather kill your own family.

11:45.371 --> 11:47.581
You can't stand the idea of failure
so you do this?

11:47.665 --> 11:48.874
[tense music continues]

11:57.174 --> 11:58.509
[breathing heavily]

12:19.155 --> 12:20.322
[sighs]

12:25.494 --> 12:26.954
[gasoline splashing]

12:35.504 --> 12:36.922
[music intensifying]

12:42.803 --> 12:43.846
[music abates]

12:44.555 --> 12:45.931
[breathes heavily]

12:56.525 --> 12:57.568
[sighs]

13:01.822 --> 13:02.698
[exhales]

13:13.125 --> 13:14.126
[softly] Yun…

13:17.338 --> 13:18.881
Where's Se-yun?

13:22.968 --> 13:24.053
[whimpers softly]

13:26.305 --> 13:28.224
[shallow, ragged breathing]

13:29.099 --> 13:30.100
My son.

13:33.103 --> 13:34.313
My son.

13:35.064 --> 13:37.817
Where is he? I wanna see Yun.

13:38.317 --> 13:39.819
[sobbing]

13:42.321 --> 13:43.656
Where is my son?

13:44.949 --> 13:46.617
Tell me he's all right.

13:48.035 --> 13:50.246
Tell me you didn't. [cries]

13:50.830 --> 13:52.414
I'm begging you.

13:52.498 --> 13:53.916
Tell me you didn't.

13:53.999 --> 13:55.125
[sobbing]

13:55.835 --> 13:57.294
How could you?

13:58.170 --> 14:01.715
How can you kill your own flesh and blood?

14:01.799 --> 14:04.009
[wails] He is our child!

14:04.093 --> 14:05.845
-[Su-hun] Get off!
-[crying]

14:05.928 --> 14:06.929
[Su-hun grunts]

14:07.638 --> 14:08.973
This is your fault.

14:09.056 --> 14:12.226
-[Eun-joo groans]
-Why couldn't you just leave it alone?!

14:14.311 --> 14:15.896
I'm doing this to protect us.

14:16.689 --> 14:17.648
[coughs]

14:18.357 --> 14:19.233
[strained gulp]

14:19.316 --> 14:21.735
-[both breathing heavily]
-[mournful music playing]

14:22.653 --> 14:23.737
[Su-hun sighs]

14:28.367 --> 14:29.410
[lighter clatters]

14:39.837 --> 14:41.088
You left me no choice.

14:42.089 --> 14:43.841
If you'd kept the secret…

14:45.885 --> 14:47.177
[labored breathing]

14:47.261 --> 14:48.220
[choking]

14:49.555 --> 14:52.808
[straining] …we could have
kept pretending our family had it all.

14:55.728 --> 14:56.937
[grunts]

14:58.981 --> 15:01.108
[mournful music continues]

15:01.191 --> 15:02.568
[muted soundscape]

15:08.365 --> 15:11.452
Su-hun, I'll kill you!

15:12.202 --> 15:14.705
If my Eun-joo dies in that fire,
I'll kill you.

15:16.790 --> 15:19.585
This isn't how the story ends.
I won't allow it.

15:21.879 --> 15:23.672
This is not how her life ends.

15:23.756 --> 15:24.840
[music fades]

15:24.924 --> 15:26.467
This is not her story.

15:26.550 --> 15:27.468
[inhales sharply]

15:27.551 --> 15:29.470
You will not kill my Eun-joo.

15:29.553 --> 15:30.763
[dramatic music playing]

15:36.060 --> 15:36.894
EMERGENCY SERVICES

15:36.977 --> 15:38.979
-[tires screech]
-[engine revving]

15:42.608 --> 15:43.484
[gasps]

15:46.904 --> 15:48.656
[tires screech]

15:49.448 --> 15:50.699
[passing car horn honking]

15:51.742 --> 15:53.494
[car horn blares]

15:53.577 --> 15:54.703
[cop 1] What the hell?

15:55.412 --> 15:56.455
Come on. Let's go.

15:56.956 --> 15:59.291
-[dramatic music continues]
-[tires screeching]

16:01.043 --> 16:03.045
[approaching police siren wailing]

16:06.382 --> 16:10.302
[cop 1 over PA] Black sedan,
license ending 6904, stop your vehicle.

16:11.595 --> 16:12.972
6904!

16:13.681 --> 16:15.349
Pull over immediately!

16:15.432 --> 16:16.809
[siren wailing]

16:16.892 --> 16:19.353
Police? I'll lead you right to it.

16:19.853 --> 16:21.563
You're gonna have to hit the gas!

16:21.647 --> 16:23.565
I'm not pulling over, okay?

16:23.649 --> 16:26.443
This is gonna destroy your life,
you sick fuck!

16:26.527 --> 16:29.154
Everyone's gonna see you
hauled away in handcuffs!

16:29.238 --> 16:30.906
[cop 1 over PA] 6904, pull over!

16:30.990 --> 16:32.157
That's an order.

16:36.036 --> 16:37.997
This guy's nuts. Let's get closer.

16:38.497 --> 16:39.623
[cop 2] Yes, sir. Gladly.

16:40.582 --> 16:42.042
[dramatic music continues]

16:43.085 --> 16:44.253
[siren wailing]

16:49.049 --> 16:51.385
-[ambulance siren wailing]
-[horn honks]

16:53.971 --> 16:55.055
[tires screech]

16:56.932 --> 16:58.600
[woman] I don't smell any smoke.

17:00.227 --> 17:01.729
-[tires screech]
-[man 1] Whoa.

17:01.812 --> 17:02.646
[Mun-oh pants]

17:02.730 --> 17:04.398
[neighbors chatter indistinctly]

17:06.150 --> 17:07.276
[panting]

17:08.986 --> 17:10.404
-Move! Move!
-[woman shrieks]

17:10.487 --> 17:11.947
[neighbors murmuring]

17:12.031 --> 17:12.990
[Mun-oh] Move!

17:15.200 --> 17:16.702
[panting heavily]

17:17.244 --> 17:18.787
[man 2] Doesn't seem to be anyone here.

17:20.039 --> 17:21.540
[fireman] We'll wait a few minutes.

17:22.332 --> 17:24.001
-When did--
-Why aren't you inside? Huh?

17:24.585 --> 17:26.503
Why are you all standing out here? Huh?

17:26.587 --> 17:28.881
Hello, sir. Are you the one
who called in the fire?

17:28.964 --> 17:30.340
I did. But who cares?

17:30.424 --> 17:33.093
Why aren't you in there putting it out
instead of asking questions?

17:33.177 --> 17:35.846
Break down the damn door!
That man's in there now!

17:35.929 --> 17:38.932
He set the whole place on fire
with his wife and son inside!

17:39.725 --> 17:41.810
Hey! Kim Su-hun!

17:41.894 --> 17:44.688
You sick bastard! I won't let you do this!

17:44.772 --> 17:47.691
-Open the door! Open the door!
-[fireman] That won't work.

17:47.775 --> 17:50.027
And there's no fire.
We don't smell any smoke.

17:50.110 --> 17:52.488
[man 3] What's going on?
We were called for multiple injuries.

17:52.571 --> 17:54.073
-Oh.
-[approaching siren wailing]

17:54.156 --> 17:56.241
It's likely a false alarm. Sorry.

17:58.077 --> 18:00.537
Are you sure…
you don't have the wrong address?

18:00.621 --> 18:01.914
You idiots!

18:02.414 --> 18:05.209
You need to get in there!
Someone's gonna die if you don't!

18:05.292 --> 18:07.294
-Go in!
-Why didn't you pull over, huh?

18:07.795 --> 18:09.963
-We've been chasing this guy.
-Let us in, crazy asshole!

18:10.047 --> 18:12.424
[cop 2] That's enough.
You own the car with the 6904 plates?

18:12.508 --> 18:14.343
Do you know
how many infractions you're in for?

18:14.426 --> 18:16.929
I wanted you to follow. I need help.

18:17.012 --> 18:19.723
You need to get in there.
Open it! Break it down!

18:19.807 --> 18:21.725
Don't just stand there! Do something!

18:21.809 --> 18:24.144
There's still time to save her.
You have to save her.

18:24.228 --> 18:26.939
I can't let her die!
I have to save Eun-joo!

18:27.022 --> 18:28.482
[whimpers] Hey!

18:28.565 --> 18:30.776
Break it before he kills her!

18:30.859 --> 18:33.195
It's Kim Su-hun.
You know who he is, right?

18:33.278 --> 18:34.696
This is his house. Okay?

18:34.780 --> 18:37.783
That crazy bastard is nothing like
the guy you see on television.

18:37.866 --> 18:41.578
He's in there killing his own family
because they know. He is!

18:41.662 --> 18:44.748
Save them and arrest him!
And break this damn door down!

18:44.832 --> 18:45.999
You need to get in there!

18:46.083 --> 18:48.168
-Break this down before it's too late!
-Sir, enough.

18:48.252 --> 18:50.796
-[Mun-oh] You won't get away with this!
-[cop 2] Calm down.

18:50.879 --> 18:52.631
-Calm down.
-Do not resist, sir. Calm down.

18:52.714 --> 18:55.759
-I need to save her. Let me go!
-[Se-yun] Prof. Heo? What's going on?

18:55.843 --> 18:56.760
[pants]

18:58.762 --> 18:59.763
Sir?

19:02.141 --> 19:04.560
What's wrong? Why are you at my house?

19:04.643 --> 19:05.811
[footsteps approach]

19:06.770 --> 19:08.021
-[Su-hun] Mun-oh?
-Huh?

19:11.733 --> 19:12.860
Heo Mun-oh?

19:18.657 --> 19:20.284
You're Heo Mun-oh, from school.

19:21.201 --> 19:22.244
[breathes shakily]

19:24.830 --> 19:26.540
Why are all these people here?

19:28.959 --> 19:30.586
[uneasy, discordant music playing]

19:34.339 --> 19:35.465
[soundscape muffles]

19:35.549 --> 19:37.509
[echoing faintly] Is something wrong?

19:39.094 --> 19:41.013
He doesn't look so good.

19:45.017 --> 19:45.934
[breath quivers]

19:46.018 --> 19:47.853
[Eun-joo echoing faintly] Mun-oh…

19:47.936 --> 19:50.063
Why are you here?

19:50.147 --> 19:51.607
[suspenseful music playing]

19:52.274 --> 19:53.275
[gasps]

19:54.276 --> 19:55.694
[frenetic jazz playing]

19:59.948 --> 20:01.491
[exhales shakily]

20:04.578 --> 20:06.163
Perhaps we should go inside

20:06.246 --> 20:10.417
while you discuss the situation
with our son's professor?

20:10.500 --> 20:11.627
[music abates]

20:11.710 --> 20:12.961
[Mun-oh breathes shakily]

20:13.045 --> 20:14.796
[uneasy, discordant music resumes]

20:16.882 --> 20:18.342
[Mun-oh breathing shakily]

20:19.343 --> 20:20.469
[music fades]

20:29.561 --> 20:31.146
[slow, listless music playing]

20:39.154 --> 20:40.322
[muffled soundscape]

20:41.615 --> 20:43.033
[listless music continues]

20:59.841 --> 21:02.302
-[tires screech]
-[trailing car honks horn]

21:03.387 --> 21:04.429
[tires screech]

21:09.226 --> 21:11.019
[breathing heavily]

21:16.316 --> 21:18.151
[uneasy, discordant music playing]

21:21.822 --> 21:23.156
LEE KANG

21:23.240 --> 21:24.283
[line ringing]

21:24.366 --> 21:25.784
You need to pick up.

21:26.994 --> 21:28.787
Pick up your phone, Lee Kang.

21:30.247 --> 21:31.415
You think I'm playing?

21:32.082 --> 21:34.126
Answer when I call you, dammit!

21:34.710 --> 21:35.711
Pick up, you shit!

21:35.794 --> 21:36.753
[line ringing]

21:38.046 --> 21:40.090
You sent me on a wild goose chase!

21:40.674 --> 21:42.718
-Eun-joo was just fine.
-[automated voice] The person…

21:42.801 --> 21:44.094
[uneasy music continues]

21:45.929 --> 21:47.389
[cell phone vibrating]

21:53.061 --> 21:55.564
PROF. HEO MUN-OH

21:56.148 --> 21:57.316
[vibrating continues]

21:59.985 --> 22:01.320
[line ringing]

22:05.574 --> 22:06.950
-[tires screech]
-Lee Kang!

22:07.951 --> 22:08.869
[music ends]

22:08.952 --> 22:09.911
Wait there!

22:10.746 --> 22:12.581
[soft, whimsical music playing]

22:13.081 --> 22:15.751
Hey! I'm talking to you!
Where are you going?

22:16.251 --> 22:18.128
We need to talk! Stop right there!

22:18.628 --> 22:21.840
-There was no fire! Hey! Get back here!
-[frenetic jazz playing]

22:21.923 --> 22:23.717
You little sh… [grunts]

22:23.800 --> 22:24.676
[Mun-oh grunts]

22:28.472 --> 22:29.431
[grunts]

22:29.514 --> 22:30.557
[panting]

22:30.640 --> 22:32.517
[grunting breathlessly]

22:33.643 --> 22:34.519
Wait!

22:34.603 --> 22:35.854
[panting heavily]

22:43.653 --> 22:44.738
[music abates]

22:48.367 --> 22:49.951
[panting wearily]

22:54.122 --> 22:55.624
[uneasy music playing]

23:00.670 --> 23:01.922
[whimpering breathlessly]

23:17.229 --> 23:18.605
Where the hell is he?

23:20.732 --> 23:22.192
[heavy breathing slows]

23:35.956 --> 23:36.957
[clasp clacks]

23:41.169 --> 23:42.629
[keypad beeping]

23:43.672 --> 23:44.631
[door trills]

23:49.386 --> 23:51.096
-[door trills]
-[shoes clatter]

23:55.600 --> 23:56.560
You packed?

23:57.853 --> 23:59.062
Are you going somewhere?

23:59.146 --> 24:00.522
[clock ticking]

24:06.361 --> 24:07.404
[sighs softly]

24:11.241 --> 24:14.119
Lee Kang? He was here earlier, is that it?

24:18.415 --> 24:19.416
[sighs]

24:20.292 --> 24:21.918
And you two enjoyed a bottle?

24:23.420 --> 24:24.337
Together?

24:26.047 --> 24:27.674
He was alone here with you?

24:28.258 --> 24:29.301
What did he say?

24:29.926 --> 24:31.261
Why did he wanna see you?

24:34.931 --> 24:36.016
I deserve an answer!

24:36.808 --> 24:37.851
What did he say?

24:38.351 --> 24:40.061
What did that little shit tell you?

24:40.562 --> 24:43.523
He's crazy! You can't believe
a word that he says!

24:45.358 --> 24:46.818
[Hyeon-suk rummaging]

24:54.618 --> 24:56.870
He didn't show up by accident, did he?

24:58.038 --> 24:59.581
This was planned, wasn't it?

25:00.373 --> 25:02.375
It wasn't for a lesson. I know that.

25:05.003 --> 25:06.004
Your smile.

25:08.173 --> 25:10.091
Are you smiling at something he said,

25:10.884 --> 25:12.219
or something you two did?

25:12.302 --> 25:13.345
[breathes shakily]

25:14.429 --> 25:17.349
Did you invite that kid in for a drink
and then into your bed?

25:26.816 --> 25:28.360
[laughs]

25:31.238 --> 25:32.822
[laughter subsides]

25:32.906 --> 25:34.282
[breathes shakily]

25:38.995 --> 25:40.497
This is… [chuckles awkwardly]

25:42.249 --> 25:44.459
This is some kind of joke, right?

25:45.961 --> 25:48.129
Kang isn't a kid. He's a young man.

25:51.049 --> 25:52.050
Yeah. So?

25:52.551 --> 25:54.678
[gentle, dreamy piano music playing]

26:04.312 --> 26:05.730
[ethereal lilting vocals]

26:16.825 --> 26:18.910
How can he be so ungrateful?

26:22.289 --> 26:24.833
A woman like you deserves to be cherished.

26:26.751 --> 26:27.794
[music intensifies]

27:02.412 --> 27:04.748
[Hyeon-suk] Feel free
to imagine what went on.

27:04.831 --> 27:07.042
-[music ends]
-Paint a picture in your head.

27:07.917 --> 27:09.336
That's what you do, isn't it?

27:10.587 --> 27:11.546
[gasps softly]

27:12.505 --> 27:13.632
What did you do?

27:16.092 --> 27:17.844
Where's this coming from, Hyeon-suk?

27:17.927 --> 27:18.928
[breath trembles]

27:19.679 --> 27:22.015
-Since when have you been--
-It's been a while.

27:23.516 --> 27:25.143
Kang reached out on his own.

27:26.102 --> 27:28.855
Because he was worried
about your obsession with Eun-joo.

27:29.939 --> 27:31.107
[gasps softly]

27:31.941 --> 27:33.151
[soft music playing]

27:35.487 --> 27:36.613
[murmurs softly]

27:48.083 --> 27:49.042
[gulps]

27:49.125 --> 27:51.086
[breathes shakily]

27:52.587 --> 27:53.713
He lied.

27:56.383 --> 27:58.593
Mentoring was just an excuse, I see.

27:59.469 --> 28:00.804
[scoffs] He used you, Kang.

28:02.806 --> 28:03.973
Both of us.

28:06.476 --> 28:08.520
You could barely call them lessons.

28:10.313 --> 28:14.067
I realized pretty quickly the professor's
interest in my story wasn't normal.

28:16.361 --> 28:18.822
And he chooses to ignore
the story that matters.

28:24.661 --> 28:26.996
You're not the woman
he wrote his book about either.

28:30.583 --> 28:31.960
I always knew that.

28:33.920 --> 28:36.047
[sighs] I just let it slide.

28:37.590 --> 28:39.551
Put it down to creative license.

28:46.641 --> 28:47.851
Are you scared?

28:50.145 --> 28:52.147
Why did you want me to know these things?

28:54.441 --> 28:55.567
[chuckles softly]

28:59.946 --> 29:01.322
-I'm not sure.
-[music ends]

29:04.200 --> 29:05.118
You tell me.

29:05.618 --> 29:07.036
[expectant music playing]

29:07.120 --> 29:09.247
[Hyeon-suk] We met
a few more times after that.

29:09.330 --> 29:11.916
We established a genuine connection.

29:12.000 --> 29:13.752
-[music fades]
-[scoffs] Jesus.

29:13.835 --> 29:17.213
That piece of shit got you
to listen to his lies? Huh?

29:21.259 --> 29:22.635
Did you have sex?

29:26.890 --> 29:28.391
That's what you're asking?

29:28.892 --> 29:30.602
That's what caught your attention?

29:32.479 --> 29:33.772
Kang is a bright one.

29:34.272 --> 29:36.357
You don't know which story really matters.

29:36.441 --> 29:38.318
You have no idea how good you've had it.

29:39.652 --> 29:42.030
Well, what story matters to you? Tell me.

29:42.697 --> 29:43.615
No need.

29:44.157 --> 29:46.618
Our stories are going their separate ways.

29:49.204 --> 29:50.455
I'm confused.

29:51.414 --> 29:52.582
Of course you are.

29:53.082 --> 29:55.293
Put in simpler terms, I'm out.

29:56.127 --> 29:58.254
I don't have the patience or the desire.

30:01.341 --> 30:04.344
I want a life where I decide what counts.

30:04.427 --> 30:06.054
[despondent guitar music playing]

30:09.641 --> 30:11.351
[high heels clatter]

30:11.851 --> 30:13.436
[footsteps departing]

30:14.938 --> 30:15.980
Don't go.

30:19.943 --> 30:21.903
-Jo Hyeon-suk.
-[front door opens]

30:23.488 --> 30:24.322
[door trills]

30:24.405 --> 30:25.490
Don't go.

30:29.452 --> 30:30.328
[door trills]

30:30.995 --> 30:32.580
[inhales deeply]

30:37.210 --> 30:38.294
[huffs shakily]

30:38.378 --> 30:39.796
[despondent music continues]

30:45.301 --> 30:47.011
[softly] Don't do this, Hyeon-suk.

30:49.305 --> 30:51.057
[tearfully] I can't live without you.

30:54.018 --> 30:55.395
Don't do this.

30:59.774 --> 31:00.859
[groans]

31:02.986 --> 31:04.237
What's happening?

31:05.947 --> 31:07.323
I lost my wife.

31:07.407 --> 31:09.284
-[music fades]
-[cell phone vibrating]

31:09.367 --> 31:10.660
What have I done?

31:11.661 --> 31:12.954
[sniffles, sobs]

31:13.037 --> 31:14.163
[vibrating continues]

31:16.541 --> 31:17.417
[sighs]

31:18.710 --> 31:19.711
[vibrating stops]

31:21.379 --> 31:22.213
Yeah?

31:22.297 --> 31:25.133
[Hyeong-jong] Mun-oh! Thank God!
I'm glad you answered my call.

31:25.216 --> 31:27.176
Have you seen the forum yet?

31:27.260 --> 31:29.053
It's really something else.

31:30.388 --> 31:31.931
That's for students.

31:33.057 --> 31:34.392
What's going on?

31:34.976 --> 31:37.687
[Hyeong-jong] Well, I'm not sure
I should be the one to tell you this.

31:37.770 --> 31:39.772
Maybe… um…

31:40.273 --> 31:42.400
Just tell me what's on the forum.

31:43.484 --> 31:44.569
Spit it out.

31:45.153 --> 31:49.532
So… Okay, maybe just a little
to give you an idea here. Uh…

31:49.616 --> 31:54.078
"Prof. Heo Mun-oh forced me
to write defamatory content

31:54.162 --> 31:56.331
regarding the author Kim Su-hun."

31:56.414 --> 31:58.625
Uh… "Blinded by jealousy,

31:58.708 --> 32:01.628
he fabricated information
and made-up scenarios

32:01.711 --> 32:05.214
with the intention
of destroying Mr. Kim's reputation."

32:05.298 --> 32:06.591
And it continues with,

32:06.674 --> 32:09.886
"Once I called him out on it,
he tried to bribe me to keep quiet."

32:09.969 --> 32:12.847
"He offered to get the test questions
for the coding competition

32:12.931 --> 32:14.015
to me in advance."

32:14.515 --> 32:16.851
"When I refused, he quit tutoring me,

32:16.935 --> 32:19.812
and he stole my work
and claimed it as his own."

32:19.896 --> 32:23.107
That's it in a nutshell.
And it was posted anonymously.

32:23.191 --> 32:25.151
They also mentioned
they're uploading a copy

32:25.234 --> 32:28.655
of the recently finished novel
as evidence of your wrongdoing.

32:28.738 --> 32:30.198
This is nuts.

32:30.281 --> 32:32.575
Views are skyrocketing
as I'm reading this,

32:32.659 --> 32:33.910
and so are the comments.

32:33.993 --> 32:35.870
It's spreading like wildfire.

32:36.371 --> 32:38.539
Is this a prank? Is there…

32:38.623 --> 32:41.000
Is there any truth to this crazy claim?

32:41.084 --> 32:42.752
[Mun-oh breathing anxiously]

32:44.337 --> 32:45.296
[disconnect tone]

32:45.380 --> 32:47.090
[tense music playing]

32:52.637 --> 32:53.471
My novel.

32:54.555 --> 32:55.890
Where's my story?

32:56.432 --> 32:57.600
It should be here.

33:00.269 --> 33:02.021
I know it's in here.

33:02.105 --> 33:03.356
[breathes frantically]

33:03.439 --> 33:04.399
Where is it?

33:05.233 --> 33:06.734
Don't tell me he took it.

33:06.818 --> 33:08.027
Was he in here?

33:10.321 --> 33:13.491
[huffs] How dare you come in here
without permission, huh?

33:14.033 --> 33:15.576
You think you can steal it?

33:16.077 --> 33:18.746
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to call is not available.

33:18.830 --> 33:20.331
-To leave a message, press one.
-What?!

33:20.415 --> 33:22.834
Steal from me! You lying son of a bitch!

33:24.419 --> 33:25.461
[cell phone trills]

33:25.545 --> 33:28.172
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to call is not available.

33:28.256 --> 33:30.174
-To leave a message, press one.
-Answer the phone!

33:30.258 --> 33:32.719
You lousy fuck! That was my work!

33:33.219 --> 33:35.596
Damn you! That was my novel!

33:35.680 --> 33:38.766
[exclaims] You stole my work! You bastard!

33:38.850 --> 33:40.309
It's my work!

33:40.393 --> 33:42.520
You don't deserve it!

33:43.021 --> 33:44.897
[grunting breathlessly]

33:44.981 --> 33:45.898
Lee Kang.

33:46.733 --> 33:48.693
Is that even your name?

33:49.485 --> 33:51.237
How could you do this?

33:52.572 --> 33:54.282
How could you do this to me?

33:54.782 --> 33:56.784
-I taught you to write!
-[music ends]

33:56.868 --> 33:59.537
Today, we have shocking updates
on the story,

33:59.620 --> 34:03.082
which started with serious allegations
that Prof. Heo Mun-oh

34:03.166 --> 34:05.960
of Yeonseo University in Seoul,
forced one of his students

34:06.044 --> 34:09.672
to write a novel slandering
best-selling author Kim Su-hun.

34:09.756 --> 34:11.007
[girl] I feel so bad for…

34:11.090 --> 34:15.344
[newscaster] Today, the novel was posted
in its entirety on the same online forum,

34:15.428 --> 34:17.889
adding more fuel
to this rumor-filled fire.

34:17.972 --> 34:21.976
Causing particular outrage is the fact
that Kim Su-hun is depicted

34:22.060 --> 34:25.688
as a philandering,
bloodthirsty psychopath.

34:25.772 --> 34:27.356
[despondent guitar music playing]

34:28.066 --> 34:29.942
[boy] He can't even write his own work.

34:30.026 --> 34:31.069
What a loser.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.154
[students chattering indistinctly]

34:50.338 --> 34:53.132
TRASH BELONGS IN THE TRASH CAN!

34:53.216 --> 34:54.300
[music rises]

34:59.847 --> 35:00.973
[sighs]

35:02.433 --> 35:05.144
[newscaster] In response,
Mr. Kim's legal representative stated

35:05.228 --> 35:08.314
that they are preparing a lawsuit,
as the novel can be considered

35:08.397 --> 35:11.567
a deliberate attempt
to defame their client's reputation.

35:11.651 --> 35:14.403
Meanwhile, Yeonseo University
has called Heo Mun-oh

35:14.487 --> 35:16.531
before the disciplinary committee.

35:16.614 --> 35:20.159
Public attention is focused on
how they will handle this situation.

35:21.953 --> 35:23.037
[woman 1 sighs]

35:27.333 --> 35:28.417
[music fades]

35:35.049 --> 35:36.134
[man 1 scoffs softly]

35:37.593 --> 35:40.304
So you're saying
this student deceived you?

35:41.222 --> 35:42.223
[scoffs]

35:43.307 --> 35:45.518
Do you think that excuses your behavior?

35:47.478 --> 35:49.605
You're the one in a position of authority,

35:49.689 --> 35:53.442
and your excuse is this measly letter
outlining your lack of responsibility?

35:56.487 --> 35:59.574
[woman 1] How do you intend to repair
the damage your actions have caused

35:59.657 --> 36:01.159
to our reputation?

36:01.242 --> 36:03.411
Your unethical behavior
has put the university

36:03.494 --> 36:06.414
under heavy and negative scrutiny
in all media.

36:07.540 --> 36:08.541
[sighs]

36:09.208 --> 36:11.794
[man 2] For most of your time here,
you've had an excellent record.

36:11.878 --> 36:14.130
But recently,
you've cancelled several classes

36:14.213 --> 36:16.174
and stopped attending faculty meetings.

36:16.674 --> 36:19.719
Moreover, you are accused of stealing
test questions from a colleague

36:19.802 --> 36:22.013
in order to help a student cheat.

36:23.848 --> 36:25.308
There's no excuse for that.

36:25.892 --> 36:30.104
What you did is not only unethical
but absolutely illegal. It's theft.

36:32.356 --> 36:34.025
[woman 1] Prof. Heo,

36:34.108 --> 36:36.360
you took Lee Kang under your wing.

36:38.487 --> 36:40.448
You mentored this student.

36:40.948 --> 36:43.451
You claim you don't have
his contact information.

36:43.534 --> 36:45.620
And Mr. Kang has asked
for a leave of absence

36:45.703 --> 36:47.705
due to the stress of the situation.

36:47.788 --> 36:48.873
[sighs]

36:49.874 --> 36:51.334
[sighs]

36:51.417 --> 36:52.585
[man 2 sighs]

36:55.671 --> 36:56.547
All right.

36:57.798 --> 37:00.968
If we accept the idea
that you were lied to and deceived

37:01.052 --> 37:03.429
by the student you chose to mentor,

37:04.263 --> 37:06.015
would you care to explain

37:06.724 --> 37:07.892
why he did it?

37:08.768 --> 37:10.478
Because there must be a reason.

37:21.364 --> 37:23.366
[somber piano music playing]

37:26.994 --> 37:28.204
[inhales shakily]

37:28.955 --> 37:30.665
[softly] I wish I could explain.

37:37.672 --> 37:39.507
But I don't know what motivated him.

37:46.180 --> 37:48.266
All I did was try to teach him.

37:51.936 --> 37:53.312
[breathes shakily]

38:02.405 --> 38:03.531
[music fades]

38:08.494 --> 38:10.496
[clock ticking]

38:14.292 --> 38:16.294
[cell phone vibrating]

38:23.926 --> 38:25.344
[exhales dazedly]

38:27.138 --> 38:28.514
[vibrating continues]

38:34.145 --> 38:35.187
[sighs]

38:36.564 --> 38:37.565
[vibrating stops]

38:40.401 --> 38:41.402
[clatters]

38:42.236 --> 38:43.279
[sighs]

38:45.656 --> 38:47.658
[cell phone vibrating]

38:54.707 --> 38:55.666
[sighs]

38:56.625 --> 38:57.543
[grunts]

38:58.502 --> 39:00.129
-[sighs]
-[vibrating continues]

39:02.423 --> 39:03.299
[vibrating stops]

39:03.799 --> 39:07.178
You have the wrong number,
so get lost and go fuck yourself!

39:07.678 --> 39:08.596
[tuts]

39:09.138 --> 39:10.056
[cell phone beeps]

39:20.649 --> 39:22.276
[object shuffles]

39:23.069 --> 39:24.153
[paper rustles]

39:25.946 --> 39:26.989
[groans]

39:38.167 --> 39:39.335
[huffs]

39:45.800 --> 39:46.926
[huffs]

39:48.844 --> 39:49.845
[grunts]

40:05.736 --> 40:06.695
Mm.

40:07.988 --> 40:08.864
[grunts]

40:17.706 --> 40:19.291
[coughs]

40:20.835 --> 40:21.836
[coughs]

40:23.087 --> 40:24.213
[vibrates]

40:34.390 --> 40:35.683
[breathes heavily]

40:41.397 --> 40:43.232
[Kang] It's been a while, Prof. Heo.

40:44.275 --> 40:45.526
This is Lee Kang.

40:46.318 --> 40:48.195
I sent you an email. You should read it.

40:48.279 --> 40:49.822
I should read it.

40:51.157 --> 40:53.659
You've got some nerve, you lying fuck.

40:54.410 --> 40:55.744
[low, tense music playing]

41:14.472 --> 41:16.390
PROF. HEO, HERE IS MY LAST ASSIGNMENT

41:17.683 --> 41:19.310
[Kang] Dear Professor.

41:19.935 --> 41:21.145
How have you been?

41:22.396 --> 41:24.565
I heard you were looking
to get a hold of me.

41:24.648 --> 41:25.483
[typing]

41:25.566 --> 41:28.068
I figure you must have a lot of questions.

41:29.236 --> 41:33.449
If you're reading this,
consider it as a reward for your patience.

41:33.949 --> 41:37.453
As my last assignment,
I'm taking you back to the beginning.

41:38.329 --> 41:39.580
[intriguing music playing]

41:39.663 --> 41:41.790
Do you remember the first time we met?

41:42.416 --> 41:43.792
It was 12 years ago.

41:46.253 --> 41:47.379
Twelve years ago?

41:52.092 --> 41:53.093
[music continues]

42:05.064 --> 42:08.275
[Hyeon-suk] We're almost there.
Do you think you can stop sulking now?

42:08.776 --> 42:10.694
You're the one who forced me to come here.

42:11.737 --> 42:13.531
Don't act surprised if I'm cranky.

42:13.614 --> 42:15.741
[tuts] You're always cranky.

42:16.242 --> 42:19.119
You've been cooped up for weeks.
You need to get out.

42:20.246 --> 42:23.290
You're in a rut.
Maybe you just need to change things up.

42:24.500 --> 42:26.377
You said you don't have any good ideas,

42:26.460 --> 42:29.171
so I thought a change of scenery
will help you get some.

42:35.302 --> 42:36.887
I didn't realize it's close to the water.

42:36.971 --> 42:38.305
-It's gorgeous.
-Enough.

42:38.806 --> 42:40.766
[scoffs] It's an orphanage.
I'm not good with kids.

42:40.849 --> 42:43.686
I'm the one working with them.
You can just sit there and read.

42:43.769 --> 42:45.688
Or go for a walk outside.

42:46.188 --> 42:48.732
This'll be fun. I'll buy you dinner after.

42:54.363 --> 42:55.364
[Hyeon-suk] Oh!

42:56.198 --> 42:58.367
-A-Are we stuck?
-[groans]

42:58.450 --> 42:59.994
-You're kidding.
-[engine revs]

43:08.544 --> 43:09.587
Crud.

43:10.170 --> 43:11.964
NEW DRIVER

43:17.636 --> 43:19.888
Honey, we're stuck in a pothole.

43:22.224 --> 43:23.309
Hold on.

43:25.269 --> 43:26.312
[groans]

43:27.980 --> 43:30.316
[grunts] Jesus.

43:34.820 --> 43:37.448
Look is what you do
when you're driving the car.

43:37.531 --> 43:38.991
Too late now.

43:41.327 --> 43:43.203
Let's hope it's not a flat.

43:48.375 --> 43:51.211
[Hyeon-suk] So when one of your friends
gives the same answer as you,

43:51.295 --> 43:53.422
you're going to put a sticker there.

43:53.505 --> 43:57.009
This is a fun way to see
how many things we have in common.

43:57.092 --> 44:00.554
When you complete a line with stickers,
you're going to yell, "Bingo!"

44:00.638 --> 44:01.639
Can you guys try it?

44:01.722 --> 44:04.558
[all] Bingo!

44:04.642 --> 44:05.684
[Hyeon-suk] Fantastic!

44:05.768 --> 44:08.395
Now let's try a question.
What's your favorite fruit?

44:08.479 --> 44:11.190
-[boy] This is for babies.
-[Hyeon-suk] Watermelon, okay.

44:12.232 --> 44:13.984
Who cares about fruit?

44:16.945 --> 44:17.780
Can I go?

44:18.697 --> 44:19.782
Sorry?

44:20.366 --> 44:22.284
Do I have to do this?

44:23.410 --> 44:25.579
No one has to do it.

44:26.622 --> 44:27.623
You can just watch.

44:27.706 --> 44:30.292
Or you can color
or play with the stickers.

44:31.168 --> 44:32.002
Hmm?

44:41.512 --> 44:42.429
[chuckles softly]

44:42.513 --> 44:43.722
[gentle music playing]

44:47.601 --> 44:48.811
[birds chirping]

45:17.715 --> 45:18.924
[sighs]

45:21.385 --> 45:22.553
[music fades]

45:24.638 --> 45:25.889
How old are you?

45:27.307 --> 45:30.227
Why do adults always ask my age?

45:31.061 --> 45:33.397
I'll tell you mine if you tell me yours.

45:33.897 --> 45:35.232
[chuckles]

45:37.484 --> 45:39.903
I asked you that 'cause I'm curious.

45:42.030 --> 45:43.407
I just turned eight.

45:47.119 --> 45:48.662
I'm wondering why

45:50.080 --> 45:52.040
you're not playing with the others.

45:54.793 --> 45:56.211
Don't you like stickers?

45:57.629 --> 46:00.799
After the games, we have to
talk about why we're here.

46:02.843 --> 46:04.511
I don't wanna do that.

46:07.723 --> 46:10.434
You mean, they want you
to talk about your parents?

46:10.517 --> 46:12.603
I said I don't wanna do that.

46:15.147 --> 46:20.152
If I share my memories with strangers,
they won't be special anymore.

46:24.406 --> 46:26.450
[duck quacking]

46:26.533 --> 46:28.577
Hmm. I see.

46:30.579 --> 46:31.580
[sighs]

46:32.331 --> 46:33.373
I have an idea.

46:34.124 --> 46:36.794
I'd like to try something with you. Hmm?

46:38.921 --> 46:39.963
Stand up.

46:40.047 --> 46:41.715
You'll need to be able to see the water.

46:43.634 --> 46:45.761
Look over there at the ducks.

46:46.261 --> 46:48.806
You see them? Let's talk about them.

46:49.306 --> 46:51.642
Enjoying a swim on a nice day.

46:52.434 --> 46:54.728
-For real?
-Mm. For real.

46:56.271 --> 46:58.148
The baby duck, we know he's the baby

46:58.232 --> 47:00.818
because he's smaller,
and he's sticking close to his parents.

47:00.901 --> 47:02.653
See? You sure?

47:02.736 --> 47:03.946
[duck quacks]

47:04.029 --> 47:05.614
That duckling is you.

47:06.281 --> 47:10.452
The other two, the one in front,
making sure he's sticking close,

47:10.536 --> 47:11.829
that one's the mama.

47:11.912 --> 47:13.080
[duck quacks]

47:13.163 --> 47:16.416
And then the bigger one,
that one's the papa.

47:18.544 --> 47:19.878
I suggest

47:20.546 --> 47:22.923
we try talking about this duck family.

47:24.299 --> 47:25.551
We'll pretend

47:26.552 --> 47:28.262
their story is yours.

47:29.888 --> 47:31.932
-Their story?
-Mm. That's right.

47:35.143 --> 47:38.397
Why do you think the duckling was annoyed?

47:38.939 --> 47:41.900
Why didn't he… wanna talk earlier?

47:44.653 --> 47:45.863
What got him

47:47.781 --> 47:49.741
so angry and quiet inside?

47:49.825 --> 47:52.077
-[duck quacking]
-[water splashing]

47:53.412 --> 47:55.122
[poignant piano music playing]

47:59.668 --> 48:00.752
[sobs]

48:05.716 --> 48:08.218
The baby duck feels alone.

48:08.302 --> 48:10.262
[crying softly]

48:11.263 --> 48:13.265
His family's gone.

48:17.144 --> 48:18.854
His parents died.

48:22.482 --> 48:23.483
He's sad.

48:24.026 --> 48:24.985
[sobs]

48:26.612 --> 48:27.821
Because…

48:31.783 --> 48:34.786
he misses them, more than he can stand.

48:36.038 --> 48:37.122
[cries]

48:37.915 --> 48:39.833
[Kang] Thanks to that man's kindness,

48:40.334 --> 48:42.628
that little boy learned about stories.

48:42.711 --> 48:44.963
Thanks to the tale about the duck family,

48:45.047 --> 48:48.050
he was able to do something
he hadn't done in a long time.

48:48.550 --> 48:50.719
Open up about his parents.

48:50.802 --> 48:52.179
[boy sobbing]

48:53.889 --> 48:58.268
The daddy duck was so strong.
His job made him like that.

48:58.769 --> 49:00.938
[Kang] Those moments
were magical for that boy.

49:01.021 --> 49:02.105
[boy chatters]

49:02.189 --> 49:04.816
[Kang] For the first time
since he'd come to the orphanage,

49:04.900 --> 49:06.818
he could talk about his mom and dad.

49:07.319 --> 49:09.363
He wasn't afraid to share his memories.

49:09.446 --> 49:10.530
[boy] …and mama duck.

49:10.614 --> 49:11.698
[music intensifies]

49:11.782 --> 49:13.158
Where would they go?

49:15.160 --> 49:18.121
They would take rides in the dad's truck.

49:18.205 --> 49:20.374
And they would have a huge picnic.

49:20.457 --> 49:21.375
[music swells]

49:21.458 --> 49:23.460
They played and laughed their heads off.

49:25.087 --> 49:28.757
The baby duck was really happy.
He had the best family.

49:29.508 --> 49:30.634
[children laughing]

49:30.717 --> 49:31.551
[music abates]

49:31.635 --> 49:34.513
Thank you again for coming.
It's so good for the children.

49:34.596 --> 49:36.556
They're so sweet. They seem happy here.

49:36.640 --> 49:39.434
I should be the one
thanking you for this session.

49:40.102 --> 49:42.437
As you know, this kind of work
goes towards my degree.

49:42.521 --> 49:44.147
You reached out just when I needed.

49:48.485 --> 49:49.820
[door opens]

49:53.323 --> 49:54.950
Thanks again. The children were wonderful.

49:55.033 --> 49:56.576
[man] Thank you. I'll pass that on.

49:56.660 --> 49:58.704
-[Hyeon-suk] Bye.
-Best of luck with your studies.

49:58.787 --> 49:59.663
[chuckles]

50:02.791 --> 50:04.126
Excuse me?

50:05.377 --> 50:07.587
Oh. Hello.

50:08.171 --> 50:09.589
I spoke to the other teacher.

50:10.257 --> 50:11.842
The other…

50:11.925 --> 50:13.802
Ah! [chuckles]

50:14.636 --> 50:17.472
Um, I was just wondering
where he went off to.

50:20.017 --> 50:21.518
You wanna say goodbye?

50:32.571 --> 50:33.655
[yells shrilly]

50:33.739 --> 50:35.699
[chuckles]

50:35.782 --> 50:37.367
You're worse than the kids.

50:43.999 --> 50:45.917
It's possible you missed your calling.

50:46.418 --> 50:49.046
That little boy
I saw you talking to outside,

50:49.129 --> 50:51.381
it sounds like you had a great connection.

50:51.882 --> 50:54.009
He was hoping to catch you just now.

50:54.092 --> 50:57.220
[chuckles] He wanted your address
so he could write to you.

50:57.304 --> 50:58.722
He wants to stay in touch.

50:59.222 --> 51:01.767
He said you showed him
how to make a good story.

51:01.850 --> 51:05.479
[chuckles] Whatever you two talked about,
you made that little boy's day.

51:05.979 --> 51:07.856
Did you give him our address?

51:07.939 --> 51:11.526
Of course I did. He was so sweet.
His name is Lee Kang.

51:11.610 --> 51:14.613
I don't wanna know who he is
or stay in touch.

51:15.113 --> 51:17.157
You were pretty interested
in his story, weren't you?

51:17.240 --> 51:18.992
I was being polite to a child.

51:19.076 --> 51:21.453
He didn't like your thing
so he walked out.

51:21.536 --> 51:24.081
I thought he'd be
a good character study, at least.

51:25.123 --> 51:27.918
But he's just an orphan. It's always
the same scenario with these kids.

51:28.001 --> 51:29.503
A car crash or some illness.

51:29.586 --> 51:33.131
Nothing special to inspire
or make one stand out above the others.

51:33.632 --> 51:34.633
[grumbles]

51:34.716 --> 51:37.135
How can you be so uncaring?

51:37.636 --> 51:39.638
How are you not inspired?

51:39.721 --> 51:42.099
All the trauma these kids
have been through so young.

51:42.182 --> 51:44.059
I know they've been through a lot.

51:44.559 --> 51:46.853
All I said is that he doesn't stand out.

51:46.937 --> 51:49.773
You need something special
for a story to really move you.

51:50.857 --> 51:52.901
Anyway, it doesn't matter. Let's go.

51:52.984 --> 51:55.987
If he sends something,
I won't bother answering. Okay?

51:56.488 --> 51:59.032
We're done.
You drove here, I'll drive back.

51:59.950 --> 52:00.909
[purse unzips]

52:01.660 --> 52:02.577
[keys jangle]

52:04.996 --> 52:06.206
[Mun-oh sighs]

52:09.042 --> 52:11.211
[despondent, instrumental music playing]

52:18.301 --> 52:20.387
YEONSEO UNIVERSITY
PROF. HEO MUN-OH, KOREAN LITERATURE

52:20.470 --> 52:21.471
[car door closes]

52:22.973 --> 52:23.974
[door closes]

52:24.724 --> 52:26.393
-[car engine starts]
-[sniffles]

52:29.396 --> 52:30.355
[music continues]

52:31.064 --> 52:33.108
[girl, faintly] One, two, three! Cheese!

52:33.191 --> 52:34.401
Okay, Dad, your turn.

52:34.901 --> 52:36.862
WELCOME, YEONSEO UNIVERSITY FRESHMEN

52:37.445 --> 52:38.947
[indistinct chattering]

52:41.825 --> 52:42.742
Do a finger heart.

52:48.123 --> 52:49.249
[music continues]

52:53.295 --> 52:55.422
PROFESSOR'S OFFICE, HEO MUN-OH

52:55.505 --> 52:57.924
[boy] Aw, man. I'm never gonna
learn my way around here.

52:58.008 --> 53:01.136
You sure it's this floor? I'm so lost.

53:02.220 --> 53:04.055
-Huh?
-[Se-yun] Oh, Prof. Heo.

53:05.348 --> 53:07.642
I have him for a writing class
this semester.

53:08.185 --> 53:11.563
[girl] I heard his classes are tough.
He's old-school, been around forever.

53:11.646 --> 53:12.939
[Se-yun] Yeah, I heard that too.

53:13.023 --> 53:15.108
He actually went to school
with my parents.

53:15.192 --> 53:19.154
He and my dad were in the same program,
'cause they both wanted to be writers.

53:20.197 --> 53:21.198
My dad was better at it.

53:21.281 --> 53:23.241
-The professor couldn't stand it.
-[girl chuckles]

53:23.325 --> 53:26.453
He wrote one book, and since then,
never wrote another word.

53:26.536 --> 53:28.955
But the funniest thing is
he had a huge crush on my mom.

53:29.039 --> 53:30.040
Used to follow her around.

53:30.123 --> 53:31.291
[tense music playing]

53:47.891 --> 53:49.100
[Velcro scratches]

53:49.184 --> 53:51.686
Oh. You're in YDOC too?

53:52.187 --> 53:53.438
I've got the same bag.

53:53.521 --> 53:55.315
[keyboard clacking]

53:57.025 --> 53:59.903
I'm Kim Se-yun.
I just started in Library Science. You?

54:00.403 --> 54:02.530
Hi. My name's Lee Kang.
Electronic Engineering.

54:02.614 --> 54:03.823
[tense music continues]

54:06.493 --> 54:07.911
[dishes clink nearby]

54:21.299 --> 54:22.300
[chuckles softly]

54:23.593 --> 54:25.512
-[boy 1] This place is huge!
-Yeah, I guess.

54:25.595 --> 54:28.765
-You guys hungry? Snacks in the kitchen.
-[Se-yun] Mom loves having people over.

54:28.848 --> 54:30.225
Yun! [chuckles]

54:35.105 --> 54:36.398
[boy 2] Oh!

54:37.190 --> 54:38.858
These are for you.

54:38.942 --> 54:41.152
-Wow. It looks so good.
-Enjoy, you guys.

54:41.236 --> 54:44.030
[Kang] By the way,
the housekeeper, Min-hui… [scoffs]

54:44.114 --> 54:45.991
…purely a figment of my imagination.

54:46.074 --> 54:47.117
Stay there.

54:47.200 --> 54:49.035
I'm sorry I ever thought
I could mentor you.

54:49.119 --> 54:50.412
-[horn honking]
-We are done!

54:50.495 --> 54:51.454
[tires screech]

54:51.538 --> 54:52.872
-[crash]
-[woman screams]

54:52.956 --> 54:54.416
[onlookers gasps and scream]

54:54.499 --> 54:56.876
-No.
-[woman] Oh my God!

54:56.960 --> 54:58.420
[panicked chatter]

54:58.503 --> 55:00.505
-[woman] Oh my God!
-[man] Call emergency!

55:00.588 --> 55:02.048
[ominous music drones]

55:04.926 --> 55:06.845
[woman] I don't know what to do.
Anyone know CPR?

55:06.928 --> 55:09.472
[Kang] At that moment,
your words came back to me.

55:11.558 --> 55:14.060
You said that for a story to stand out,

55:15.603 --> 55:18.940
it had to have something special
that really moves you.

55:20.400 --> 55:21.776
[shakily] So that woman…

55:25.238 --> 55:26.489
Is Min-hui.

55:26.573 --> 55:27.991
[frenetic jazz playing]

55:28.074 --> 55:28.992
The one who's hurt?

55:29.075 --> 55:30.410
And he's there.

55:31.369 --> 55:33.413
-Who is? Where?
-[woman] Is that blood?

55:33.496 --> 55:35.290
[indistinct, panicked chatter]

55:46.259 --> 55:47.635
That's Se-yun's dad?

55:49.137 --> 55:50.263
He's the one

55:51.890 --> 55:53.224
you've been writing about?

56:02.442 --> 56:03.318
[music stops]

56:03.401 --> 56:04.527
[Kang] The accident…

56:04.611 --> 56:05.987
[unsettling music playing]

56:06.654 --> 56:08.198
…was a lucky coincidence.

56:08.281 --> 56:10.116
[woman 1 pants] Mr. Kim!

56:10.617 --> 56:13.119
-There you are. Go with her.
-Of course.

56:13.620 --> 56:16.247
-[woman 2] Oh my God.
-Can I go with her? She works with us.

56:16.748 --> 56:19.042
-Thank you. Thank you.
-[woman 2] Oh my God. What happened?

56:19.125 --> 56:20.585
[frenetic jazz resumes]

56:22.754 --> 56:23.755
[music abates]

56:39.396 --> 56:40.688
[entry bell jangles]

56:41.272 --> 56:42.148
Hello.

56:42.232 --> 56:43.525
[intriguing music playing]

56:44.776 --> 56:45.610
Professor.

56:47.112 --> 56:50.573
While we're not friends,
he's not a complete stranger either.

56:51.074 --> 56:52.033
However,

56:52.659 --> 56:54.327
to help you with your studies,

56:54.828 --> 56:57.414
I think continuing… our individual…

56:57.497 --> 57:01.042
[Kang] From then on,
I wasn't writing the story anymore.

57:01.126 --> 57:03.128
-You were.
-And for you, and for me too.

57:03.211 --> 57:05.046
[foreboding, discordant music playing]

57:06.381 --> 57:07.298
[man] Kang,

57:07.966 --> 57:10.093
what's with that look on your face lately?

57:10.593 --> 57:13.555
Something on your mind?
You know you can tell me.

57:14.097 --> 57:15.181
[Kang sighs]

57:15.265 --> 57:16.224
[gulls calling]

57:16.307 --> 57:18.059
I'm trying to wrap up a project.

57:19.352 --> 57:20.645
But I'm almost finished.

57:21.271 --> 57:23.565
It sounds like a pretty big deal.

57:24.441 --> 57:28.570
If it's stressing you out,
you don't have to come visit.

57:29.571 --> 57:31.489
You should focus on your work.

57:33.783 --> 57:36.244
It's my job to make sure
you're all right, isn't it?

57:37.787 --> 57:39.122
Because you're family.

57:40.623 --> 57:42.375
You're like my second dad.

57:42.876 --> 57:44.210
Or like a mother hen.

57:44.294 --> 57:45.670
[laughs]

57:45.753 --> 57:46.880
You're so full of it.

57:47.505 --> 57:50.049
I know you called me "the drill sergeant"
behind my back.

57:50.133 --> 57:52.844
But kids always think
their parents don't know these things.

57:52.927 --> 57:54.304
[laughs]

57:56.389 --> 57:58.099
[soft, somber piano music playing]

58:07.775 --> 58:08.735
[Kang] So…

58:08.818 --> 58:10.570
[music rises, turns orchestral]

58:10.653 --> 58:12.822
…how's your story these days?

58:14.365 --> 58:17.869
[Mun-oh] Just shut your mouth!
It's not lying if you know it's the truth.

58:17.952 --> 58:20.872
And the truth is,
Su-hun went to meet the letter-writer.

58:22.040 --> 58:23.500
[chuckles giddily]

58:23.583 --> 58:24.709
[breathes heavily]

58:24.792 --> 58:26.419
[keyboard clacking rapidly]

58:30.882 --> 58:32.133
[continues typing]

58:33.259 --> 58:34.928
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

58:35.011 --> 58:36.179
BY HEO MUN-OH

58:37.597 --> 58:38.640
[sighs]

58:41.226 --> 58:42.810
[Mun-oh] I finally did it.

58:42.894 --> 58:44.437
[exhales deeply]

58:44.938 --> 58:45.897
Heo Mun-oh…

58:45.980 --> 58:47.273
[sobs]

58:47.357 --> 58:48.900
…your second novel.

58:51.236 --> 58:52.362
[sniffles]

58:53.029 --> 58:54.280
[exhales]

58:56.241 --> 58:57.283
[music continues]

58:57.367 --> 58:58.368
[Kang] So…

59:00.912 --> 59:03.164
how's your story these days?

59:08.878 --> 59:10.296
Is it special?

59:10.380 --> 59:11.381
[music fades]

59:11.881 --> 59:13.550
Are you enjoying it?

59:18.930 --> 59:19.889
[hesitates]

59:21.849 --> 59:22.976
[sighs]

59:23.059 --> 59:24.018
[glasses clatter]

59:25.270 --> 59:26.729
That damn kid.

59:28.982 --> 59:30.233
Well played.

59:35.863 --> 59:36.781
Well played!

59:36.864 --> 59:38.283
[manic laughter]

59:42.620 --> 59:43.746
[sighs]

59:48.293 --> 59:49.252
[chuckles]

59:51.504 --> 59:53.089
[chuckling]

59:57.176 --> 59:58.970
[laughing]

01:00:01.639 --> 01:00:03.224
[laughter turns into weeping]

01:00:14.902 --> 01:00:17.071
[solemn, orchestral music playing]

01:00:18.364 --> 01:00:19.324
[groans]

01:00:24.704 --> 01:00:26.039
You little shit.

01:00:28.875 --> 01:00:29.709
[murmurs softly]

01:00:32.211 --> 01:00:33.671
This goes back to that?

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:40.845
The three ducks.

01:00:40.928 --> 01:00:42.138
[laughing]

01:00:45.850 --> 01:00:47.101
[crying]

01:00:54.400 --> 01:00:55.401
[whimpers]

01:00:56.819 --> 01:00:58.071
[groans]

01:00:59.572 --> 01:01:01.074
[crying]

01:01:05.411 --> 01:01:07.705
[screams]

01:01:07.789 --> 01:01:08.831
I trusted you!

01:01:08.915 --> 01:01:10.249
[solemn music continues]

01:01:24.931 --> 01:01:25.973
[music fades]

01:01:26.057 --> 01:01:26.933
[exhales softly]

01:01:35.733 --> 01:01:37.443
[low, unsettling music playing]

01:01:38.444 --> 01:01:40.530
What do you think, Professor?

01:01:42.198 --> 01:01:43.282
[music rising slowly]

01:01:43.366 --> 01:01:45.034
Do you think it stands out?

01:01:56.879 --> 01:01:58.047
[music fades]

01:02:08.433 --> 01:02:09.684
[Mun-oh munching]

01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:21.028
[gulps, exhales deeply]

01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:28.911
[keyboard clacking]

01:02:46.220 --> 01:02:47.346
[door chime jingles]

01:02:56.856 --> 01:02:58.107
[keyboard clacking]

01:02:59.734 --> 01:03:01.736
[footsteps approaching slowly]

01:03:12.413 --> 01:03:14.081
Faust. Hmm.

01:03:14.165 --> 01:03:17.335
People are still willing
to tackle the classics, huh?

01:03:18.836 --> 01:03:21.714
You'll enjoy it more
if you look into how it was written.

01:03:23.132 --> 01:03:24.300
How are you paying?

01:03:26.677 --> 01:03:27.887
[keyboard clacking]

01:03:27.970 --> 01:03:30.223
-[Kang] I know how it was written.
-[typing stops]

01:03:32.308 --> 01:03:34.644
It evolved over a 60-year period.

01:03:35.311 --> 01:03:37.605
It spanned most of the author's life.

01:03:45.738 --> 01:03:47.031
[low, uneasy music playing]

01:03:47.114 --> 01:03:48.574
[breathing shakily]

01:03:51.118 --> 01:03:53.287
[fingers strumming on book]

01:04:23.651 --> 01:04:24.652
I need help

01:04:25.945 --> 01:04:27.196
to get my story out.

01:04:33.369 --> 01:04:35.663
I could use some professional guidance.

01:04:37.123 --> 01:04:38.499
[uneasy music intensifies]

01:04:43.337 --> 01:04:44.964
[music abates, fades]

01:05:07.612 --> 01:05:08.779
What's the story?

01:05:09.280 --> 01:05:11.490
-[frenetic jazz playing]
-[scoffs softly]

01:05:20.207 --> 01:05:21.709
-[chuckles softly]
-[music peaks]

01:05:21.792 --> 01:05:23.419
[music abates, fades]

01:05:23.502 --> 01:05:25.129
[Kang] It's to be continued.

01:05:26.047 --> 01:05:26.964
[chuckles softly]

01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:29.050
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

01:05:29.133 --> 01:05:30.968
[lively, rousing jazz playing]

01:07:54.528 --> 01:07:55.654
[music fades]
